        <item>
            <title>1.5</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 01:19:08 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.5</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[Fix incorrect download resolution, added Re-Encode options for dowmloads, and UI bug fixes

## What's New
- Convert can now automatically re-encode incompatible sources to H.264 or HEVC for compatability issues
- Drop's own version is now shown in the log at launch
- Added a choice of H.264, HEVC, or Off when a download needs to re-encode for compatibility

## Changed
- Condensed repetitive progress lines in the Log tab into one self-updating line

## Fixes
- Fixed 4K+ YouTube downloads silently saving at a lower resolution than requested
- Fixed the progress indicator briefly overlapping the Reveal/Redownload buttons when a download finishes
- Fixed Convert's bottom bar visually glitching when clearing or resizing the queue]]></description>
